From: leondgarse <leondgarse@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 15:02:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] fix(tbmv): correct ctbmv strided-incx handling and diag
 UB sizing

- normalise/restore x into a contiguous logical-order buffer for incx != 1,
  so every compute path stays on the simple stride-1 layout
- diag kernel: size the staging buffer for 32B-padded strided loads
- diag kernel: use GatherMask for the dense x load (tables are for strided)

All 1872 cases pass on Ascend910B3 / CANN 9.1.0:
12 enum combos x 13 shapes x incx in {1,2,-1,-3} x 3 lda paddings.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BgUmdszSh9vJscPMXn433N
---
